numerical_example:
Simple Example (4 Points on a Line: 1, 2, 8, 9):

1. Start:
   • Four separate clusters: {1}, {2}, {8}, {9}

2. Step 1 (Merge closest pairs):
   • Distance between 1 and 2 is 1 -> Merge into {1, 2}
   • Distance between 8 and 9 is 1 -> Merge into {8, 9}

3. Step 2 (Measure distance between remaining groups):
   • Minimum cross-cluster distance is |2 - 8| = 6

4. Step 3 (Final merge):
   • {1, 2} and {8, 9} merge at distance 6 into {1, 2, 8, 9}

5. Cut the tree:
   • Cut at height 3: Gives 2 clusters -> {1, 2} and {8, 9}
   • Cut at height 7: Gives 1 cluster -> {1, 2, 8, 9}
